{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"707d7798-68ee-45a1-b0ec-0396348f3299","title":"A system of two linear equations as crossing lines"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"707d7798-68ee-45a1-b0ec-0396348f3299","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Each point on this line satisfies the first equation. We want a point that also satisfies a second equation.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Two equations, one solution"},{"op":"equation","id":"first_eq","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=2x+1"},{"op":"figure","id":"lines","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-1,4],"y":[-2,7],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"rising","y":"2*x+1","domain":[-1,3],"label":"y = 2x + 1"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"707d7798-68ee-45a1-b0ec-0396348f3299","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The second equation gives another line. Where the lines cross, the same x and y satisfy both equations.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"second_eq","anchor":{"el":"first_eq","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=-x+4"},{"op":"figure","id":"second_line","on":"lines","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"falling","y":"-x+4","domain":[-1,4],"label":"y = −x + 4"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"707d7798-68ee-45a1-b0ec-0396348f3299","step":{"id":"s3","script":"At the crossing, both expressions for y are equal. Solving gives x equals one, then y equals three: the system's solution.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"solve","anchor":{"el":"second_eq","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"2x+1=-x+4\\;\\Rightarrow\\;3x=3\\;\\Rightarrow\\;x=1"},{"op":"figure","id":"crossing","on":"lines","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"solution","at":{"hit":["rising","falling"]},"label":"(1, 3)"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"solution"},"to":[1,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"solution"},"to":[0,3],"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"check","anchor":{"el":"solve","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"2(1)+1=3=-1+4\\qquad (x,y)=(1,3)"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Why is the crossing point a solution to both equations?","expected_gist":"It lies on both lines, so its coordinates satisfy both equations."}}}
